%N A037629 Base 8 digits are, in order, the first n terms of the periodic sequence with initial period 2,3,0.
%H A037629 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (8,0,1,-8)
%F A037629 G.f.: x*(2+3*x) / ( (x-1)*(8*x-1)*(1+x+x^2) ). - _R. J. Mathar_, Nov 21 2011
%F A037629 From _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 20 2026: (Start)
%F A037629 a(n) = floor(19*8^(n+1)/511).
%F A037629 a(n) = 8*a(n-1) + a(n-3) - 8*a(n-4). (End)
%t A037629 Table[FromDigits[PadRight[{},n,{2,3,0}],8],{n,25}] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Jan 28 2019 *)
%o A037629 (PARI) a(n) = 152*8^n \ 511; \\ _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 20 2026
